abstract=f'''Hexapod route planning must balance distance, destination time, nominal battery capacity, and terrain difficulty within a finite computational allowance. This article evaluates a resource constrained pipeline combining safe corridor initialization, visibility search, continuous waypoint refinement, and geometry checked tracking. A common evaluator prefers feasible routes before a declared weighted score. The original frozen study contains 1,232 attempts on 24 primary test worlds; a separate 800-attempt replication finds identical routes for an adaptive search candidate and the retained V4 planner. A final prospective campaign adds 1,200 scheduled records, six planner configurations, and 48 fresh primary worlds, equally divided between standard and predeclared shifted conditions. Controls execute Open Motion Planning Library 2.0.1 RRT*, RRT* with a common incumbent, and RRTConnect, alongside individually tuned polished particle swarm and ant colony methods. The proposal admits {P['proposed_v4']['admitted']} of 96 primary attempts. Its world averaged paired score improvements are {C['pso_polished']['mean_relative_percent']:.2f}% and {C['aco_polished']['mean_relative_percent']:.2f}% against the polished swarm controls, conditional on joint admission. Alternative weights and shorter allowances test preference and budget sensitivity. Exact saved-route physics replays yield {safe['successful']}/12 successful proposal missions with the revised follower, compared with {legacy['successful']}/12 using the legacy follower. All ties, losses and rejected plans remain in the evidence. The contribution is an evaluated engineering integration with explicit trade-offs; universal planner superiority, unassisted locomotion, and measured electrical savings are not established.'''
assert 150<=len(abstract.split())<=250,len(abstract.split())
text=re.sub(r'(?s)(@ABSTRACT\n).*?(\n\n@KEYWORDS)',lambda m:m[1]+abstract+m[2],text,1)
text=text.replace('## VII Discussion and Limitations','## IX Discussion and Limitations').replace('## VIII Conclusion','## X Conclusion')
text=text.replace('The primary evaluation contains 864 planning attempts on 24 fresh worlds.','The original primary evaluation contains 864 planning attempts on 24 fresh worlds.')
text=text.replace('## II Related Work','Two additional frozen campaigns broaden the evidence without replacing the original outcomes. A replication evaluates an adaptive candidate on 48 new test worlds; the final campaign evaluates actual external planners, objective-weight sensitivity, shifted procedural conditions, and exact saved-route tracking on another 48 test worlds. V6 identifies this final pipeline and protocol, while the focal route optimizer remains V4. These are separately planned parameter-selection and evaluation studies, not neural-network training [@evidence].\n\n## II Related Work',1)
text=text.replace('Sampling based optimal motion planning provides another important family of alternatives [@rrtstar], but is outside the implemented baseline set. Conclusions are restricted accordingly.','Sampling based optimal motion planning provides another important family of alternatives [@rrtstar]. It was absent from the original campaign; the final campaign adds actual OMPL RRT* and RRTConnect implementations [@ompl], [@rrtconnect]. Their inner additive cost relaxation and common final evaluator are distinguished in Section VIII. These controls expand coverage without representing an exhaustive OMPL benchmark.')
